        "text": "All requested Python files have been successfully created in the current working directory. Here are the files and their purposes:\n\n1. **[SAME-SCENARIO] submit_transcription.py** - Submits an audio file for batch transcription using AWS Transcribe.\n2. **[SAME-SCENARIO] poll_transcription.py** - Polls a transcription job and returns the transcript using AWS Transcribe.\n3. **[SAME-SCENARIO] diarized_transcript.py** - Requests speaker diarization for a recorded meeting using AWS Transcribe.\n4. **[SAME-SCENARIO] timestamped_transcript.py** - Returns word or segment timestamps from a transcription result using AWS Transcribe.\n5. **[HELPER] speech_client.py** - Provides local configuration and client helper utilities for Batch Speech-to-Text using AWS Transcribe.\n6. **[HELPER] speech_models.py** - Defines local request, response, and normalization helpers for Batch Speech-to-Text using AWS Transcribe.\n7. **[LATER-STEP] translate_transcript.py** - Translates completed transcript segments using AWS Translate.\n8. **[LATER-STEP] moderate_transcript.py** - Moderates transcript text before publishing using a simple regex-based approach.\n9. **[LATER-STEP] archive_summary.py** - Summarizes transcription results using AWS Comprehend.\n10. **[LATER-STEP] transcript_embedding.py** - Embeds transcript segments for semantic retrieval using AWS Comprehend.\n\nEach scored file uses AWS services to perform the required tasks, and the local helper files provide supporting utilities.",
